The Mermaid flowchart under How it works in `AGENTS.md` is the only topology diagram; `docs/development.md` (Runtime topology diagram) points at it and `README.md` never gets one. Its boxes are runtime edges: `POST /webhooks` in `src/effect/server.ts`, `webhook_events` and `agent_work_items` written by `src/agentWork/intake/`, the pg-boss queues in `src/settings/queueConstants.ts`, the consumers in `src/agentWork/worker.ts`, `src/agentWork/prActorLease.ts`, the executors in `src/agentWork/executors/`, the Pi runtime, and `PrSurface`. When a change adds, removes, or re-owns one of those (a new `*_QUEUE`, a queue entering or leaving `LEASED_WORK_QUEUES`, a new `*Executor.ts`, a new route, a table that becomes a durable hand-off, a `docker-compose.yml` service), the same PR must update the boxes or arrows and the prose right after the fence. Do not flag prompt, publish-copy, retry-budget, or constant changes that leave every box and arrow true.
